{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260916-46e5fedc555dc4545b647549","sequence":3,"timestamp":"2026-09-16T18:53:47.858719Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"38aa51b0-1202-4351-b87d-37b76b6553ce"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"STORY-260916-73a5zg","element_type":"story"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260916-4006c1771a46896d2394808e","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":"Finding E5 (Medium): environments §9.5 detects a foreign-manager symlink and allows takeover with backup, but no sentence forbids writing through an existing link at a managed-surface path. The reference implementation had exactly this defect during EPIC-260905 (takeover wrote through a dotfile-manager symlink into the foreign source of truth) and fixed it locally; an implementation written from the text alone reproduces it."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Finding E5 (Medium): environments §9.5 detects a foreign-manager symlink and allows takeover with backup, but no sentence forbids writing through an existing link at a managed-surface path. The reference implementation had exactly this defect during EPIC-260905 (takeover wrote through a dotfile-manager symlink into the foreign source of truth) and fixed it locally; an implementation written from the text alone reproduces it.\n\nImplementation verification (TASK-260916-dv7xv5 rev2, curator main 80483355, launcher main b34e1e27, static): mitigated in code for the inspected case, spec rule absent. The copied root-context write removes the target first (switch.go:523-530, fallback :539-545) and replaceLink removes before os.Symlink (:694-696). Limits: remove-then-create is not O_NOFOLLOW and not race-free; writeStoreDocument still uses plain os.WriteFile (:686); other managed writes were not inspected. The manager task is a vector plus an atomicity review covering those writes."}}]}
